THE 2003.11 FAIL AND THE SKIPPED 2003.10 -- framework drift, not 6.2.40 (compared against d4c21f7 as the queue requires)
  Device side, all PASS (verbatim):
    Bootup Stage 2 Diagnostics Menu: ... 4. Erase FLASH (Filesystem only) ... -> "WARNING: This option will
    destroy the contents of the FLASH file system. Press Y to proceed" -> y -> "Erasing nand0: [=====...]"
    19:34:14 PASS: device erased flash successfully
    19:37:04 ...saw bootup complete messages on swi_a : "done!" / PASS: Device rebooted successfully
    19:37:24 PASS: swi_a contains no exceptions
  Harness side:
    19:37:18 Set the swi_a boot configuration back to the TestSet configuration (flash:/swi_a_5700_2003.cfg)
    swi_a(config)# boot conf swi_a_5700_2003.cfg -> "% flash:/swi_a_5700_2003.cfg does not exist or is inaccessible"
    19:37:21 !!FAIL: TestSet configuration file flash:/swi_a_5700_2003.cfg missing from swi_a
    19:37:33 Setup is no longer reliable - all devices will be rebooted -> Power cycle swi_a completed: Success
    19:41:14 !!! TestSet configuration file missing from one or more devices, skip any remaining TestCases
    -> 2003.10 ("Boot stage 2 Diagnostics menu, option 2. Test FLASH (Filesystem only)", added tear=False, runs
       after .11) NOT RUN.
  Why it differs from Feb (sources read, /home/st-art/framework read-only, `git -c safe.directory=... show`):
    - test-5700.2003.py TestCase_11.tear_down() sets `self.doConfCheck = False` (line 511): the erase is
      deliberate, so the case opts out of the config restore/compare.
    - Framework d4c21f7 (Feb): the "Set ... boot configuration back to the TestSet configuration" step lives in
      _PostTearDownThread, called from _post_tear_down() only `if self.doConfCheck:` -> skipped for 2003.11; Feb's
      2003.11 log has no such line and ends PASS (3/0), and 2003.10 then PASSed.
    - Framework now (HEAD 89900a6, 2026-10-06 17:40; the queue recorded a5bb6a1 at triage -- the live framework
      moved 3 commits during this run): since c1e7679 (2026-09-17, Blair Wilson, "SYST-9408 ... split TestCase tear
      down into separate steps") ATTestCase.__run calls `self._pre_tear_down_reset_boot_config()` under
      `if self.doTear:` BEFORE tear_down() and regardless of doConfCheck ("run this even if aborted ...").
      So after the deliberate erase the reset runs, finds no TestSet cfg, fails the case and flags
      testSetConfigurationFileMissing, which makes ATTestSet skip the rest of the TestSet.
  => 2003.11's own checks all PASSED; the FAIL and the 2003.10 skip are a harness/script interaction introduced by
     framework c1e7679, not a bootloader 6.2.40 result.
  Side effects of the erase (expected, accepted in the queue): flash emptied (releases, cfgs, default.cfg, and the
  ACCESS licence -- 2004's setup logged "Add ACCESS license to swi_a" again); next boot "Warning:
  flash:/default.cfg does not exist, loading factory defaults." (x2); no forced-password dialog occurred.

